I see the problem! After reading "hello\n", we get EOF on the next fgetc call. But `feof(fp)` returns false because we haven't tried to read past EOF yet. So we continue and add a NUL byte at position 0, returning an empty string with len=0. Then we loop again, fgetc returns EOF immediately, but feof is still false! This creates an infinite loop.

The fix: after reading data and hitting EOF (len > 0), we should return that data. But when we hit EOF on the first read (len == 0), we should return NULL to signal end of file.
